---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Ruby Smythe"
  description="How this site handles your data: no accounts, no forms, no cookies, and cookieless analytics."
>
  <main class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 13 September 2026</p>

    <p>
      This site is the portfolio of Ruby Smythe, a tattoo artist and painter in
      Edinburgh. It collects as little as possible. There are no accounts, no
      contact forms, and no newsletter.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      I use Vercel Web Analytics and Speed Insights to see which pages get
      visits and how quickly they load. Both are cookieless. They do not follow
      you across other sites, they do not build a profile of you, and they only
      report aggregate numbers. Your IP address is processed in memory to count
      a visit and is not stored next to your browsing.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      Vercel hosts this site. Like most hosts, Vercel keeps short-lived server
      logs that include IP addresses, so it can keep the site online and block
      abuse. Vercel's privacy policy explains how it handles that data.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>This site sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device.</p>

    <h2>Instagram</h2>
    <p>
      The contact links on this site lead to Instagram. Once you follow one,
      you are on Meta's site and Meta's privacy policy applies. I only see the
      messages you choose to send me there. If you want a message deleted, ask
      me in that conversation and I will remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under UK GDPR you can ask what personal data I hold about you, ask me to
      correct or delete it, and object to how I use it. In practice that means
      messages you have sent me. You can reach me on Instagram at
      <a
        href="https://www.instagram.com/byrubydesigns"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">@byrubydesigns</a
      >. If you are unhappy with how I respond, you can complain to the
      Information Commissioner's Office at
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>

    <p class="legal-back"><a href="/">Back to the portfolio</a></p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
